<title>POLAND: BPH, PBK banks grant loan for power plant.</title>
<headline>BPH, PBK banks grant loan for power plant.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy SA (BPH) and Powszechny Bank Kredytowy SA (PBK) will extend a 95.6 million zloty ($29.2 million) syndicated loan for the Siersza SA power plant, BPH said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that BPH will grant 53.2 percent of the loan and PBK 47.7 percent.</p>
<p>The loan, extended for 11 years, will be used to finance the construction of desulphurisation devices at the Siersza plant, based in the southern town of Trzebinia.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 ($ = 3.272 Polish Zlotys)</p>
